{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01CMMGL4gHVLWzWZBzn4iggb","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Section 8: Observability & Analytics\n2\t\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t## Q1\n6\t\n7\t**Problem framing**\n8\t\n9\tCheckout funnels are multi-step flows where users drop off at every stage. Without precise event instrumentation you can't tell whether users abandon at address entry, payment entry, or order review — meaning you optimize blindly. Granular events with consistent properties let you compute step-level conversion, run cohort analyses, and A/B-test individual stages.\n10\t\n11\t**Approach**\n12\t\n13\tDefine one event per discrete funnel boundary. Each event carries a shared \"envelope\" of properties plus step-specific ones.\n14\t\n15\t```typescript\n16\t// Shared envelope attached to every checkout event\n17\tinterface CheckoutEventBase {\n18\t  session_id: string;          // anonymous, per-tab\n19\t  checkout_id: string;         // idempotency key for this cart attempt\n20\t  user_id?: string;            // logged-in users only\n21\t  experiment_variants: Record<string, string>; // active A/B flags\n22\t  device_type: 'mobile' | 'tablet' | 'desktop';\n23\t  timestamp_ms: number;\n24\t}\n25\t\n26\t// --- Step events ---\n27\t\n28\t// Fired when checkout page first renders (before Stripe init)\n29\ttrack('checkout_started', {\n30\t  ...base,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6f204bf-32e1-4fe7-87b7-580f13b36e45","uuid":"f5c6be97-797e-4d51-9ec3-9da986d7e34a","timestamp":"2026-06-20T19:33:10.045Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sarthakagarwal/Desktop/projects/prep/system-design/payments-system/answers/08-observability-analytics.md","content":"# Section 8: Observability & Analytics\n\n---\n\n## Q1\n\n**Problem framing**\n\nCheckout funnels are multi-step flows where users drop off at every stage. Without precise event instrumentation you can't tell whether users abandon at address entry, payment entry, or order review — meaning you optimize blindly. Granular events with consistent properties let you compute step-level conversion, run cohort analyses, and A/B-test individual stages.\n\n**Approach**\n\nDefine one event per discrete funnel boundary. Each event carries a shared \"envelope\" of properties plus step-specific ones.\n\n```typescript\n// Shared envelope attached to every checkout event\ninterface CheckoutEventBase {\n  session_id: string;          // anonymous, per-tab\n  checkout_id: string;         // idempotency key for this cart attempt\n  user_id?: string;            // logged-in users only\n  experiment_variants: Record<string, string>; // active A/B flags\n  device_type: 'mobile' | 'tablet' | 'desktop';\n  timestamp_ms: number;\n}\n\n// --- Step events ---\n\n// Fired when checkout page first renders (before Stripe init)\ntrack('checkout_started', {\n  ...base,","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1111}}}
